<title>INDIA: India Reliance surges on bonus news.</title>
<headline>India Reliance surges on bonus news.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Reliance Industries Ltd surged in early trade on Friday at Bombay exchanges buoyed by the petrochemicals giant's decision to consider a bonus equity issue on June 26, brokers said.  </p>
<p>At 0515 GMT Reliance share was up 16 rupees, or 4.69 percent, to 356.50 -- a new 52-week high -- at the Bombay Stock Exchange after rising six percent on Thursday following the announcement.</p>
<p>Traders expect a bonus ratio of three shares for every five, the same as it gave 14 years ago.</p>
<p>The share was up 15 rupees, or 4.38 percent, at 357 on the rival National exchange.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
